    }
  ],
  "minor_polish": [
    "The claim of a '~1700σ discrepancy' is derived from a zero prediction and may be considered hyperbolic; a simple statement that the mass gap is non-zero would suffice.",
    "The phrase 'the only eigenvalue is the constant mode' should be corrected or removed; the Lichnerowicz operator has a continuous spectrum.",
    "References for Bekenstein–Hawking and Hawking–Page identifications lack precise definitions linking them to arithmetic of imaginary quadratic fields; these should be clarified or removed as they appear ad-hoc.",
    "The Bayesian evidence aggregation uses strong prior assumptions (e.g., uniform priors on decade ranges) that could be debated; this is not an error per se, but may be worth noting."
  ],
  "confidence": "HIGH"
}

